hen `archiver-utils` floated glob to `10.5.0`, it fell through to the \"unexpected\" bucket and exited 1 despite npm succeeding.\n     - Rewritten with a `package|title|url` allowlist:\n     ```bash\n     # \"<package>|<title>|<tracking url>\". One entry per reviewed package name.\n     #\n     # glob is pulled in by two independent chains, so it is attributed to the one\n     # we can actually act on: @link-assistant/web-capture -> archiver@7.0.1 ->\n     # archiver-utils@5.0.2 -> glob@10.5.0. (electron-builder separately pulls\n     # glob@7.2.3.) Upstream deprecated every glob below 12.x, including the very\n     # releases that fix CVE-2025-64756, so the warning is unavoidable noise rather\n     # than an actionable vulnerability -- see isaacs/node-glob#644.\n     reviewed_deprecations=(\n       \"inflight|electron-builder upstream deprecation|https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-builder/issues/10016\"\n       \"rimraf|electron-builder upstream deprecation|https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-builder/issues/10016\"\n       \"boolean|electron-builder upstream deprecation|https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-builder/issues/10016\"\n       \"lodash.isequal|electron-builder upstream deprecation|https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-builder/issues/10016\"\n       \"prebuild-install|vsce upstream deprecation|https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-vsce/issues/1290\"\n       \"whatwg-encoding|vsce upstream deprecation|https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-vsce/issues/1290\"\n       \"glob|archiver/electron-builder upstream deprecation|https://github.com/isaacs/node-glob/issues/644\"\n     )\n     ```\n     - Name extraction (after fixing my own bash bug):\n     ```bash\n     deprecated_package_name() {\n       local line=\"$1\" spec name\n       spec=\"${line#*npm warn deprecated }\"\n       spec=\"${spec%%:*}\"\n       # Strip the trailing @version. Removing the *last* '@' preserves a leading\n       # @scope, so \"@scope/pkg@1.2.3\" yields \"@scope/pkg\" and \"glob@10.5.0\" yields\n       # \"glob\". Guard the case where npm printed no version at all.\n       name=\"${spec%@*}\"\n       printf '%s' \"${name:-$spec}\"\n     }\n     ```\n     - Classification loop:\n     ```bash\n     while IFS= read -r line; do\n       case \"$line\" in\n         \"\") continue ;;\n         *\"npm warn deprecated \"*)\n           package=\"$(deprecated_package_name \"$line\")\"\n           classified=0\n           for entry in \"${reviewed_deprecations[@]}\"; do\n             if [[ \"${entry%%|*}\" == \"$package\" ]]; then\n               rest=\"${entry#*|}\"\n               trace \"classified '$package' as ${rest%%|*}\"\n               echo \"::notice title=${rest%%|*}::${line#npm warn } See ${rest#*|}\"\n               classified=1\n               break\n             fi\n           done\n           if [[ \"$classified\" == \"0\" ]]; then\n             trace \"deprecation for '$package' is not on the reviewed allowlist\"\n             printf '%s\\n' \"$line\" >>\"$unexpected\"\n           fi\n           ;;\n         *) trace \"unrecognized diagnostic: $line\"; printf '%s\\n' \"$line\" >>\"$unexpected\" ;;\n       esac\n     done <\"$stderr_log\"\n     ```\n     - Verbose mode (default OFF, per user requirement):\n     ```bash\n     verbose=\"${INSTALL_NODE_DEPENDENCIES_VERBOSE:-0}\"\n     trace() {\n       [[ \"$verbose\" == \"1\" ]] || return 0\n       printf 'install-node-dependencies: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs`** (MODIFIED — root cause C fix, `trailer_values` at ~line 149)\n     - Why: `version-and-commit.rs` calls `record_self_hosting_release` and `exit(1)`s on error, so a mis-parsed trailer fails the whole Auto Release job.\n     - Was: `let format = format!(\"%(trailers:key={key},valueonly,separator=%x1f)\");`\n     - Now:\n     ```rust\n     /// Collects `key: value` trailers from a commit message.\n     ///\n     /// This deliberately scans the whole commit body instead of using git's\n     /// `%(trailers:key=...)` placeholder. Git only recognises the *last* paragraph\n     /// of a message as the trailer block, so a blank line between two trailers\n     /// makes every trailer above it invisible. Release commit\n     /// 59650f2b45ebebf29ed67d33c9a19c1e82e7c003 separated its `Formal-AI-Session`\n     /// and `Formal-AI-Evidence` trailers with a blank line, git reported only the\n     /// evidence trailer, and the resulting \"must record both\" error failed the\n     /// whole Auto Release job (issue #796).\n     fn trailer_values(repo: &Path, commit: &str, key: &str) -> Result<Vec<String>, String> {\n         let body = git(repo, &[\"show\", \"-s\", \"--format=%B\", commit])?;\n         let prefix = format!(\"{key}:\");\n         Ok(body\n             .lines()\n             .filter_map(|line| {\n                 let line = line.trim();\n                 // Trailer keys are case-insensitive per `git interpret-trailers`.\n                 line.get(..prefix.len())\n                     .filter(|candidate| candidate.eq_ignore_ascii_case(&prefix))\n                     .map(|_| line[prefix.len()..].trim())\n             })\n             .filter(|value| !value.is_empty())\n             .map(str::to_owned)\n             .collect())\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`tests/unit/ci-cd/issue_796.rs`** (CREATED — 5 tests) — drives the real script against a fake `npm` written into a temp sandbox dir prepended to PATH. Tests: `reviewed_deprecations_are_matched_by_package_name_not_pinned_version` (uses the exact glob@10.5.0 line from run 29681451142), `unreviewed_diagnostics_still_fail_the_build`, `scoped_package_names_are_parsed_without_losing_the_scope`, `verbose_tracing_exists_and_is_off_by_default`, `the_classifier_does_not_pin_versions_in_its_allowlist` (asserts the allowlist block contains no `@`).\n\n   - **`tests/unit/ci-cd/mod.rs`** (MODIFIED) — added `mod issue_796;` after `mod issue_742;`\n\n   - **`tests/unit/specification/self_hosting_metric.rs`** (MODIFIED) — added before `release_pipeline_and_ledger_remain_pinned_to_the_metric`:\n     ```rust\n     /// Regression for issue #796: release commit 59650f2b separated its two\n     /// trailers with a blank line. ...\n     #[test]\n     fn trailers_are_recognized_even_when_separated_by_blank_lines() {\n         let repo = fixture_repo();\n         ...\n         commit(&repo, \"formal ai change\\n\\nFormal-AI-Session: spaced-session\\n\\nFormal-AI-Evidence: docs/evidence/session.txt\");\n         let measurement = metric_script::measure(&repo, \"v1.0.0\", \"HEAD\").expect(\"measurement must succeed\");\n         assert_eq!(measurement.self_authored_commits, 1, \"a blank line between trailers must not hide the session trailer\");\n         fs::remove_dir_all(repo).expect(\"fixture directory must be removed\");\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`changelog.d/20260719_130000_issue_796_ci_false_positives.md`** (CREATED) — `bump: patch`, with `### Fixed` entries for both root causes and `### Added` for the verbose env var.\n\n   - **`dev/log/issues/796/pulls/797/`** (CREATED) — `README.md` (index table + summary), `timeline-and-root-cause.md` (full timeline, 3 root causes, R1–R9 requirement table, upstream reports list, regression coverage), `template-gap-analysis.md`, `online-research.md`; plus `ci-logs/run-{29680908415,29681451142,29686858791,29686071628}.log` and `raw/` (issue/PR/run JSON, `commit-59650f2b-message.txt`, `glob-dependency-chain.txt`, `main-runs.json`).\n\n   - **`.gitkeep`** — DELETED (its own content stated \"This file will be removed when the task is complete\").\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n\n   - **My own bash bug:** First version of `deprecated_package_name` used `printf '%s' \"@${spec:1%@*}\"` — invalid bash mixing substring and suffix-removal expansion. Fixed by using `name=\"${spec%@*}\"; printf '%s' \"${name:-$spec}\"`, which correctly yields `@scope/pkg` for scoped and `glob` for unscoped, guarding the no-version case. Ver