ets needed).\n\n   Both bugs were reproduced independently (a case-statement simulation and a clean git fixture repo) before fixing, and both regression suites were confirmed to **fail against the pre-fix scripts** — the trailer test reproducing the production error string verbatim (\"must record both Formal-AI-Session and Formal-AI-Evidence\").\n\n   Verified R6 by grepping: only one `%(trailers` call site, no npm install in workflows outside the shared script, only one version-pinned allowlist.\n\n   All checks pass: `cargo fmt --check` clean, `bash -n` ok, `cargo test --test unit ci_cd::` → 111 passed (including pre-existing `issue_730` assertions on the modified script), `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features` clean. Committed as a5b9d597 and pushed.\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n   - The single genuine user message was the initial task directive (reproduced in full detail in section 1 above): solve issue #796 on branch `issue-796-9da6718935fa`, compile logs/data into `./dev/log/issues/796/pulls/797`, do deep analysis with online research, reconstruct the timeline, list every requirement, find root causes, propose solutions, check for existing components/libraries, add verbose/debug output with **default state switched off** if data is insufficient, report issues to other GitHub projects when the issue belongs to them (with reproducible examples, workarounds, and code fix suggestions), and \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\" Plus the embedded workflow guidelines (push only to `issue-796-9da6718935fa`, update PR 797 rather than creating a new one, run `gh pr ready 797` when finished, merge default branch in, verify CI passing, reproduce before fixing).\n   - The final user message instructed: respond with TEXT ONLY, no tool calls, producing this analysis and summary.\n\n   No security-relevant constraints or prohibited operations were stated beyond the